<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.00%" pitch="-2.50%">
      Then the Psalm lets the Shepherd lead us further in.<break time="500ms"/>
      He makes me lie down in green pastures.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He leads me beside still waters.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Notice how gentle those movements are.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not driving.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not scattering.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not shouting from a distance.<break time="500ms"/>
      He makes room for rest, and He leads toward calm.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Green pastures are not frantic places.<break time="500ms"/>
      Still waters are not dangerous waters.<break time="500ms"/>
      The Psalm speaks of provision that is quiet enough for a sheep to trust.<break time="1800ms"/>

      There is grass enough.<break time="500ms"/>
      Water gentle enough.<break time="500ms"/>
      Time enough to lower the head and breathe.<break time="1800ms"/>

      A sheep can only drink where the water is calm enough to trust.<break time="500ms"/>
      So the Shepherd does not merely point toward water from far away.<break time="500ms"/>
      He leads beside still waters, where fear can loosen and thirst can be met.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Pasture and water are not rewards for a sheep that has proved itself.<break time="500ms"/>
      They are provision from the Shepherd for creatures that need to be fed and settled.<break time="1800ms"/>

      This is what the Shepherd is like in the Psalms.<break time="500ms"/>
      He does not only rescue after panic.<break time="500ms"/>
      He also prevents panic.<break time="500ms"/>
      He leads to places where the nervous body can settle.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Rest is part of His guidance.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Peace is not separate from His provision.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You do not have to create still waters for yourself tonight.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
